    907  f111				   CaveLine
    908  f111							; --- Player sprite: color for THIS line, graphics byte for NEXT line ---
    909  f111							; GRP0 written on line S displays on line S+1 (latched at the sprite's
    910  f111							; window start after the write) — index graphics with A0+1 ($ff wraps
    911  f111							; to 0 = row0 on the line before the sprite).
    912  f111							; CORRECTED 2026-10-22 (Phase 4): that "line S+1" is only true for a
    913  f111							; sprite whose pixels come AFTER the store. Per Stella's Player::grp /
    914  f111							; updatePattern, a GRP write lands in myPatternNew and renders at once, so
    915  f111							; the boundary is the sprite's own pixel start (cycle ~(61+X)/3). With
    916  f111							; VDELP0=1 (set in the VBL, see the comment there) the live pattern is
    917  f111							; `myPatternOld`, latched by the GRP1 store at c58, so P0 is correct for
    918  f111							; every X < 113 px and its art row r sits on the SAME scanline as
    919  f111							; PlayerColTable[r] (COLUP0 lands at c19, before all pixels) — i.e. the
    920  f111							; art and its per-row colours finally agree. Do not reorder the colour
    921  f111							; path behind the graphics: COLUP0 must stay the first store in the body.
    922  f111							; Running-Y: Y = A0 = Scanline - RoomY is computed ONCE at kernel entry
    923  f111							; (sec/sbc RoomY/tay); .Line's iny advances it (Y = A0+1 after the
    924  f111							; graphics write = A0 of the next line). Nothing between rows may touch
    925  f111							; Y — the water-strip band-color read is an inlined `lda` (Y untouched).
    926  f111							; Cycle budget — MEASURED (sim_frame_budget, bugs.md #29 Class A):
    927  f111							; the old worst path (in-window color/beam/GRP0 + object in-range) was
    928  f111							; 78c: WSYNC write landed 2c into the next line -> full-line stall ->
    929  f111							; +1 scanline on every frame whose object window overlapped the A0=11
    930  f111							; line (24 stalls in the SIM_LEVEL=2 window, always even frames —
    931  f111							; SelectActiveObject parity rotation). Root fix: the color/beam gate
    932  f111							; below stops at A0=10; row 11 inherits row 10's COLUP0/ENAM0 writes
    933  f111							; (PlayerColTable [10]==[11], verify_build asserts) because
    934  f111							; GRP0 row11 is fetched on line A0=10 already ("row11 shows via
    935  f111							; line10"). Worst path measured 2026-10-15 (vcrunch jitter hunt):
    936  f111							; in-window color/beam/GRP0 + object in-range = 69c between WSs,
    937  f111							; start-to-start d=72 — was 73/76 (= stall zone 74-76, whole-screen
    938  f111							; +1-line jitter) until the dead `cpy #12 / bcs .GrpZero` (4c, never
    939  f111							; taken on the A0<=10 color path) moved to .GrpSkip. Budget: work
    940  f111							; <= 70c / d <= 73 — a 74-76 segment stalls a full scanline.
    941  f111							; ObjSprites+107 must stay in ONE page (else lda ObjSprites,X
    942  f111							; page-crosses, +1c on the GRP1 fetch) — verify_build enforces this.
    943  f111							; Branch targets all same-page (3c taken) and PlayerColTable in $F8xx
    944  f111							; (verify_build guards the A0=10 page-cross budget).
    945  f111							; GRP1 object section clobbers X (ObjSprites index) — row counter lives in
    946  f111							; RowIdx and X is reloaded after bne. Row-advance +6c on the .Row setup
    947  f111							; scanline (segment 63c -> 69c <= 76c): frame length unchanged.
    948  f111							; The old Scanline/sec/sbc/tay prefix cost 10c more (body 66c -> WSYNC
    949  f111							; write on cycle 76 = one cycle late): WSYNC stalled a full line per
    950  f111							; overlapping scanline — stretched cave row, HUD pushed down, and with
    951  f111							; GRP1 flicker rotation the frame length alternated (one-tile oscillation).
