    962  f115							; window in LaserHitTestBody keeps rows RoomY+2..3 = superset of the
    963  f115							; draw). In-window path only (Y<=11), so outside the window ENAM0 keeps
    964  f115							; its last write ($00 at A0=10) — no HUD artifact. verify_build asserts
    965  f115							; bit1 is set at index 2 and nowhere else, and that rows 10/11 stay equal
    966  f115							; (the A0=11 gate skip inherits row 10's writes).
