   2864  f9c1							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   2865  f9c1							; PositionBallM1 — D6 asymmetric objects, BOTH positioned in one VBL call.
   2866  f9c1							; WHY here: pre-pad headroom is 1B — inline ball+m1 (22B) cannot live in the
   2867  f9c1							; VBL block, so the ball block became this jsr and the body sits in the
   2868  f9c1							; $F9C4..$FBF7 fill (ReturnPad pin at $FBF8 unaffected; F6-safe:
   2869  f9c1							; $F9C4 & $1FFF = $19C4 ∉ $1FF4-$1FF7; bank0-only, not a fold twin).
   2870  f9c1							;   Temp	   = staged BallX (bank2 StageBandTab): 0 = symmetric → skip.
   2871  f9c1							;		     selector 4 = HMBL/RESPBL, ball x drawn clocks [A-7,A].
   2872  f9c1							;   M1X ($B0) = the async M1 block's X (staged by the room load; 0 = none).
   2873  f9c1							;   It must be its OWN byte: CollisionEndX is the laser wall-clamp's
   2874  f9c1							;   scratch and a leftover there drew a phantom M1 dash (2026-10-22).
   2875  f9c1							;		     0 = no M1 patch → skip.
   2876  f9c1							;		     selector 3 = HMM1/RESM1, left-col block x = 7+8*col
   2877  f9c1							;		     (passed to SetObjectXPos as M1X+1 — Stella draws 8-wide
   2878  f9c1							;		     M1 one clock left of the [A-7,A] player contract).
