   3824  fdd1							; BombTick `jsr` lands here (bank0), `sta $1FF6` switches to bank2, the `jmp`
   3825  fdd1							; is fetched from bank2's byte-identical mirror at this same address and
   3826  fdd1							; lands on the body at $FD87 (the lamp type-check reads enemy records that
   3827  fdd1							; live in bank2). Body tail-jmps ReturnPad ($FBF8); A = 1 kill (BombTick
   3828  fdd1							; awards +50 — pads cannot nest), 0 none. Old inline body ($F87F, 66B)
   3829  fdd1							; deleted: the region re-packs into the gap before the $FBD6 fold pin
   3830  fdd1							; (pre-pad headroom stays 1B — pins absorb upstream shrink, not the org).
   3831  fdd1							; TWIN: bank2.asm mirrors these exact 6 bytes at $FDD8 (the pad after
   3832  fdd1							; .HOVdone). The PickPlayerFrame pin that used to absorb the size is gone
   3833  fdd1							; (retired 2026-10-20); the $FC49 / $FBF8 pins bound this block today.
